<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Ali is a 54-year-old man with young-onset Parkinson&apos;s disease, diagnosed twelve years ago, who comes for his periodic preventive visit four weeks after his six-month Parkinson&apos;s disease review. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. He takes carbidopa-levodopa one and a half tablets three times a day, 30 minutes before meals, with an alarm on his phone, and has missed no doses. He has had no falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays this year. He walks or rides a stationary bicycle and does his physical therapy balance exercises about 180 minutes a week, and practices his voice exercises daily. He has no new concerns. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 54</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays this year</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Carbidopa-levodopa on time with phone alarms; no over-the-counter medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Parkinson&apos;s disease, Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5, without dyskinesia or wearing-off; soft speech, improved after speech therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities of daily living; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds at the six-month review</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with his spouse; close family and friends; busy schedule of public and charitable appearances, which he enjoys</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>No alcohol (AUDIT-C 0); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>About 180 minutes a week of walking, stationary cycling, and balance exercises</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; takes levodopa 30 minutes before meals and spreads protein through the day</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night; no dream enactment; not sleepy in the daytime</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; buttoning and handwriting slow</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; staff help with travel arrangements</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Grab bars in the shower, night lights, no loose rugs; smoke detectors working</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls this year</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No hearing concern; small print slower to read; no eye examination on record in recent years</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; drives only short local trips in daylight; no firearms in the home</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

