    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic preventive visit, age 54</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, anxiety, and alcohol screens are negative. Ten-year cardiovascular risk is about 5 percent by the pooled cohort equations, with no risk factor that would call for a statin. HbA1c 5.4 percent. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Parkinson&apos;s disease, Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5 (G20.A1)</content>. Stable on carbidopa-levodopa 150 mg three times daily, with no dyskinesia or wearing-off and no falls. [S]<list><item>Continue carbidopa-levodopa without change.</item><item>Next quarterly Parkinson&apos;s disease review in about two months, and the yearly movement disorders review in the spring.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypokinetic dysarthria with soft speech (R47.1)</content>. Easier to hear since speech therapy; keeps up daily voice practice. [S]<list><item>Continue daily voice exercises; refresher speech therapy if his voice softens again.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>124/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 192, HDL 50, LDL 118, triglycerides 120 mg/dL. Ten-year risk about 5 percent with no diabetes, hypertension, dyslipidemia, or smoking, so a statin is not recommended; repeat in five years</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>HbA1c 5.4 percent; overweight adult aged 35 to 70; repeat in three years</td></tr><tr><td>Healthy weight and activity</td><td>Completed today</td><td>BMI 27.7; counseled to keep up 150 minutes or more of weekly exercise, which also helps his balance and gait</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No prior screening on record. Options discussed; he chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test, and a kit was given today. A positive test needs colonoscopy</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision-making about PSA testing is recommended from age 55; to be discussed next year</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 3 at the first visit this year</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GAD-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening recommended for all adults in these age ranges; no prior result on record; drawn with his consent today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel recommended for all adults; drawn with today&apos;s blood tests</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; a single dose is recommended for adults 50 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; he will get it at the pharmacy next week</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No dose on record in the past ten years; to be given with the second zoster dose</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 75 and older, and from 50 with conditions that raise risk; his Parkinson&apos;s disease is not causing swallowing or breathing problems. Review yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Referred</td><td>No dental visit on record; Parkinson&apos;s disease calls for a dental examination every six months; appointment arranged</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Due</td><td>No eye examination on record in recent years; a comprehensive eye examination advised</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds at the six-month review; exercise and home-safety measures continue</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Quarterly Parkinson&apos;s disease review in about two months. Second zoster dose and the Tdap booster in two to six months. Dental appointment arranged. Return the stool test kit within two weeks. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
